{"type": "message", "id": "8abe6c00", "parentId": "f19ad860", "timestamp": "2026-04-08T04:02:41.584Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "tool_web_search_LpvRbXD1epSSH9aWQNyf", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"\\\"Kentucky\\\" OR \\\"Arizona\\\" OR \\\"South Carolina\\\" OR \\\"Kansas\\\" NAEP 2022 grade 8 math score\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 5,\n  \"tookMs\": 920,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"401de17ab349cc23\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n2022 MATHEMATICS STATE SNAPSHOT REPORT KENTUCKY  GRADE 8  PUBLIC SCHOOLS\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"401de17ab349cc23\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://nces.ed.gov/nationsreportcard/subject/publications/stt2022/pdf/2023011KY8.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4c00b83c6f59dbce\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNOTE: The NAEP mathematics scale ranges from <strong>0 to 500</strong>. Results presented in this report are based on public school students only.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"4c00b83c6f59dbce\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"nces.ed.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"15dc254ce0a43d7e\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n2022 MATHEMATICS STATE SNAPSHOT REPORT KANSAS  GRADE 8  PUBLIC SCHOOLS\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"15dc254ce0a43d7e\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://nces.ed.gov/nationsreportcard/subject/publications/stt2022/pdf/2023011KS8.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"83712f42db103145\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNOTE: The NAEP mathematics scale ranges from <strong>0 to 500</strong>. Results presented in this report are based on public school students only.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"83712f42db103145\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"nces.ed.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"26536e1140a49752\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe New NAEP Scores Highlight a Standards Gap in Many States - FutureEd\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"26536e1140a49752\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.future-ed.org/the-new-naep-scores-highlight-a-standards-gap-in-many-states/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"cb124c5e2ca2d377\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nForty-seven states improved NAEP math proficiency rates between 2022 and 2024 in fourth grade and 36 states did so in eighth grade. But proficiency rates remain below 2019 levels in 34 states in fourth-grade and in all but one state in eighth-grade. Similarly, math proficiency rates rose on nearly every state’s standardized tests during the same period. While state math scores declined dramatically between 2019 and 2022, particularly in eighth grade, only in Arizona, Arkansas, Florida, Idaho, and Vermont in fourth grade and Arkansas, Michigan, and Missouri in eighth grade did state test scores decline between 2022 and 2024.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"cb124c5e2ca2d377\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"February 10, 2025\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.future-ed.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"8e27c0fee22dc3b2\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNOVEMBER 2022\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"8e27c0fee22dc3b2\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://csgsouth.org/wp-content/uploads/QofM-November.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a57b34367b12b256\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nProcess (NAEP). 2022 Mathematics Assessment.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a57b34367b12b256\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"csgsouth.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e99fe4d21905b3cc\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nNAEP scores for 2022 show largest drops ever recorded in 4th and 8th grade math | WVXU\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e99fe4d21905b3cc\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.wvxu.org/education/2022-10-24/naep-scores-2022-drops-4th-8th-grade-math\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"db68c1e15cdcf8ff\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nFully 21 of the 26 urban districts managed the same in eighth-grade reading, with only Shelby County, Tennessee, Jefferson County, Kentucky, Guilford County, North Carolina, and Cleveland, Ohio, experiencing statistically significant drops. In Los Angeles, the nation’s second-largest district, eighth-grade reading performance even improved. Michael Petrilli, who leads reform-oriented Thomas B. Fordham Institute, nevertheless took a dark view of the overall NAEP outcomes.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"db68c1e15cdcf8ff\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"October 24, 2022\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.wvxu.org\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}], "details": {"query": "\"Kentucky\" OR \"Arizona\" OR \"South Carolina\" OR \"Kansas\" NAEP 2022 grade 8 math score", "provider": "brave", "count": 5, "tookMs": 920, "externalContent": {"untrusted": true, "source": "web_search", "provider": "brave", "wrapped": true}, "results": [{"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"401de17ab349cc23\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\n2022 MATHEMATICS STATE SNAPSHOT REPORT KENTUCKY  GRADE 8  PUBLIC SCHOOLS\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"401de17ab349cc23\">>>", "url": "https://nces.ed.gov/nationsreportcard/subject/publications/stt2022/pdf/2023011KY8.pdf", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"4c00b83c6f59dbce\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nNOTE: The NAEP mathematics scale ranges from <strong>0 to 500</strong>. Results presented in this report are based on public school students only.\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_