{"type": "message", "id": "29cb53e5", "parentId": "ff6b033e", "timestamp": "2026-04-08T04:03:12.464Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "tool_exec_ufVFst1cR9hVBjJMXccL", "toolName": "exec", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "xrdb: Can't open display ''\n/root/.bashrc: line 16: bind: warning: line editing not enabled\n• In 2022, the average score of eighth-grade students in Kansas was 272. This was not\nsignificantly different from the average score of 273 for students in the nation.\n• The average score for students in Kansas in 2022 (272) was lower than their average\nscore in 2019 (282) and in 2000 (283).\n• The percentage of students in Kansas who performed at or above the NAEP Proficient\nlevel was 23 percent in 2022. This percentage was smaller than that in 2019 (33\npercent) and in 2000 (34 percent).\n• The percentage of students in Kansas who performed at or above the NAEP Basic\nlevel was 61 percent in 2022. This percentage was smaller than that in 2019 (71\npercent) and in 2000 (76 percent).\n\nNAEP ACHIEVEMENT-LEVEL PERCENTAGES AND AVERAGE SCORE\nRESULTS\nKansas\n\nAverage Score\n\n2000\n\n24*\n\n2019\n\n43*\n\n29*\n--\nCOMPARE THE AVERAGE SCORE IN 2022 TO OTHER STATES/\nJURISDICTIONS\n\nAVERAGE SCORES FOR STATE/JURISDICTION AND THE NATION (PUBLIC)\nScore\n500\n\nAK\n\nME\nVT\nWA\n\nMT\n--\nIn 2022, the average score in Kansas (272) was\nlower than those in 19 states/jurisdictions\nhigher than those in 9 states/jurisdictions\nnot significantly different from those in 23 states/jurisdictions\n\n'05\n\n'07\n\n'09\n\n--\n• In 2022, Black students had an average score that was 29 points lower than that for\nWhite students. This performance gap was not significantly different from that in 2000\n(43 points).\n• In 2022, Hispanic students had an average score that was 20 points lower than that\nfor White students. This performance gap was not significantly different from that in\n2000 (24 points).\n• In 2022, male students in Kansas had an avera